{
  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_000_cost_tuned_scale_1p30",
  "intuition": "The parent loss has an extra cost-gap term (-0.1*gap) added inside the logits before logsigmoid, which can already shift margins. With limited pairing signal, a slightly smaller `scale` reduces overconfident saturation after the clamp and keeps gradients in a healthier range, improving stability while still preserving the ordering pressure from (lpw-lpl).",
  "pseudocode": "scale=1.30; x = clamp(alpha*scale*(lpw-lpl) - 0.1*stopgrad(cost_b-cost_a), -20, 20); loss = -logsigmoid(x); return mean(weight*loss)",
