{
  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_002_label_smooth",
  "intuition": "The original pairwise -logsigmoid(x) can become very flat for large positive x and overly punitive for large negative x, which can hurt stability and generalization under noisy preference pairs. I add a small label-smoothing style mixture: (1-eps)*(-logsigmoid(x)) + eps*(-logsigmoid(-x)). This keeps the same pairwise structure but prevents overconfident updates and maintains gradients on both sides, improving validation objective in practice when pairs are imperfect.",
